 n<li>Compare the two graphs. Explain what the transformation has changed i
 n the conditional distribution of the dependent variable.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2
  style="border-bottom: 2px solid #333333\; padding-bottom: 6px\; margin-to
 p: 40px\;">Problem 5 — What Changes and What Remains Invariant?</h2>\n<p
 >Consider the following three Data Generating Processes:</p>\n<table style
 ="width: 100%\; border-collapse: collapse\; margin: 20px 0\;">\n<thead>\n<
 tr style="background-color: #f5f5f5\;">\n<th style="padding: 10px\; border
 : 1px solid #cccccc\;"></th>\n<th style="padding: 10px\; border: 1px solid
  #cccccc\;">Marginal generation of X</th>\n<th style="padding: 10px\; bord
 er: 1px solid #cccccc\;">Conditional generation of Y</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>
 \n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style="padding: 10px\; border: 1px solid #cccccc\;"><
