 math>"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ol type="a">\n<li>Write the theo
 retical economic relationship associated with each DGP.</li>\n<li>Generate
  100 observations from each DGP in R. Represent the three samples graphica
 lly using the <strong>same limits for the horizontal and vertical axes</st
 rong>.</li>\n<li>Compare DGP 1 and DGP 2. Which part of the marginal–con
 ditional decomposition changes? Which part remains invariant?</li>\n<li>Co
 mpare DGP 2 and DGP 3. Which part changes? Which part remains invariant?</
 li>\n<li>For each comparison\, state whether the theoretical economic rela
 tionship has changed.</li>\n<li>Explain in your own words why two populati
 ons may have very different distributions of the explanatory variable <img
  class="equation_image" title="X" src="https://um6p.instructure.com/equati
 on_images/X" alt="X" data-equation-content="X" loading="lazy" x-canvaslms-
 safe-mathml="<math xmlns=&quot\;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot\;>
 \n  <mi>X</mi>\n</math>"> while sharing the same theoretical economic rela
 tionship between <img class="equation_image" title="X^*" src="https://um6p
 .instructure.com/equation_images/X%255E%257B%252A%257D" alt="X^*" data-equ
 ation-content="X^*" loading="lazy" x-canvaslms-safe-mathml="<math xmlns=&q
 uot\;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot\;>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>X</mi>\
 n    <mo>&amp\;#x2217\;<!-- ∗ --></mo>\n  </msup>\n</math>"> and <img cl
 ass="equation_image" title="Y^*" src="https://um6p.instructure.com/equatio
 n_images/Y%255E%257B%252A%257D" alt="Y^*" data-equation-content="Y^*" load
 ing="lazy" x-canvaslms-safe-mathml="<math xmlns=&quot\;http://www.w3.org/1
 998/Math/MathML&quot\;>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>Y</mi>\n    <mo>&amp\;#x2217\;<
 !-- ∗ --></mo>\n  </msup>\n</math>">.</li>\n</ol>\n<div style="backgroun
 d-color: #f5f5f5\; border-left: 5px solid #333333\; padding: 16px 20px\; m
 argin-top: 40px\;">\n<h3 style="margin-top: 0\;">Before submitting</h3>\n<
 p>Your PDF should contain:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>your answers to all five problem
 s\;</li>\n<li>all requested R code\;</li>\n<li>all requested numerical res
 ults\;</li>\n<li>all requested graphs\;</li>\n<li>brief explanations where
  interpretation is requested.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style="margin-bottom: 0\;">S
